      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A more formal statement of these arguments follows. The probability that a specific gene from the $ P_{2} $ is incorporated into a specific line after $ k $ generations of backcrossing is $ p_{k} = (1/2)^{k+1} $. If $ n $ freely segregating factors are responsible for the character difference between the $ P_{1} $ and $ P_{2} $, then the probability that a derived line retains just one of the $ P_{2} $ alleles is",
